    "https://careers.werecruit.io/en/escp-business-school/offers/events-and-student-experience-executive-maternity-cover-24d263": {
      "title": "Events and Student Experience Executive (Maternity Cover) F/M",
      "description": "Events and Student Experience Executive (Maternity Cover) F/M - Temporary contract 5 months in London | Découvrez nos offres With your agreement, We Recruit and our partners use cookies or similar technologies to store, access, and process personal data like your visit on this website, IP addresses and cookie identifiers. Some partners do not ask for your consent to process your data and rely on their legitimate business interest. You can withdraw your consent or object to data processing based on legitimate interest at any time by clicking on “Learn More” or in our Privacy Policy on this website. View our 8 partners Learn More → Disagree and close Agree and close Menu Company page Espace Carrière & Mobilité des salariés ESCP Plus Recrutement en Europe Site ESCP See our jobs EN EN FR Company page Espace Carrière & Mobilité des salariés ESCP Recrutement en Europe Site ESCP EN Retour EN EN FR See our jobs Events and Student Experience Executive (Maternity Cover) F/M Apply to this job Events and Student Experience Executive (Maternity Cover) F/M I apply Published on               \n                16/10/2026 Subsidiary : ESCP Business School London Campus Contract type: Temporary contract\n- 5 months Work time: Full time Location London Salary 34083 GBP (£) - 35460 GBP (£) / year The company ESCP Business School was founded in 1819. The School has chosen to teach responsible leadership, open to the world and based on European multiculturalism. Six campuses in Berlin, London, Madrid, Paris, Turin and Warsaw are the stepping stones that allow students to experience this European approach to management. Job Details Salary: £34083 to £35460 per annum, dependent on experience Type of Employment: Fixed Term to 16th April 2027 (Maternity Cover) Hours: 35 hours per week (1.0 FTE) Working Location: Working predominantly on site due to the nature of the role Reporting to: Events and Student Experience Manager JOB SUMMARY AND PURPOSE The Events and Student Experience Executive will be responsible for delivering the London Campus strategic and reputational events programme for the school. These events support cross-departmental objectives, including profile-raising, enhancing the School’s reputation and content generation, promoting campus careers activities, and supporting student and alumni engagement and lifelong advocacy. Our audiences and events are hugely varied, acting as an ambassador for the School, the postholder will coordinate a wide range of events; including graduations, galas, festivals, open days, conferences, and student society activities and other more bespoke event programmes. ensuring professional & high-quality delivery. They will also support the use of School facilities for internal and external events, liaising with stakeholders throughout the booking and delivery process. This is a varied and demanding role that requires a proactive & professional self-starter with strong organisational, interpersonal, and problem-solving skills, able to manage multiple priorities with accuracy and professionalism. Flexibility is essential, as some events take place during evenings and occasionally at weekends. MAIN DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Deliver the annual strategy and plan for the School and student societies events (mix of virtual, hybrid and face to face) Play a key role in the implementation of alumni, students societies, staff and sports events calendar, which supports the School-wide objectives. Management of the day-to-day activities and logistics related to the School’s events and student societies programme (ie. Booking rooms, room set-ups, etc). Ensuring the London events calendar and diaries up to date and liaise with all departments to ensure the accuracy of each department’s activities Ensure events are executed to the highest standards, to deadline and on budget, seeking final sign off for all costs related to the event budget. Assist with the company’s presence at external events organised by industry partners Develop and produce marketing and event materials—including invitations, social media content, set design, delegate lists, badges, feedback forms, and promotional assets—ensuring alignment with the School’s brand guidelines. Actively contribute and prepare for event-planning meetings with different stakeholders, ensuring event administration is organised, accurate and follows established policies and procedures. As well as setting up and dismantling spaces for event-related activities. Represent the Events team during induction days, recruitment webinars and any other relevant events while providing outstanding customer service in support of the customer-experience expectations of the School. Thorough communication of events information with the Senior Digital Communications Manager for sharing on ESCP website Communicate with attendees to request/chase information for event projects such as company information, photos, logos, and adverts. Collaborate closely with team members and other departments across the school to enable cross-department working, sharing of intelligence and expert advice, identifying new opportunities and stronger development of the ESCP London Campus Monitor process systems and practices in place for events delivery, plan and carry out regular reviews to identify opportunities for improvement in light of changing needs, feedback and/or current best practices Ensure health & Safety and Risk assessments are thoroughly followed Student Societies: Assist in the development and management of society processes, ensuring effective and efficient delivery of a range of innovative, inspirational opportunities for students. Ensure societies are deployed in a worldly wise and targeted manner to reach a wide range of student groups giving students the opportunity to create and join shared-interest student group societies and support their maintenance and growth of societies and assist in the reporting and analysis of their work. Collect effective and accurate data and ensure key society success stories, metrics, and targets are recorded. Plan events and activities for societies to help their growth and development. This will include assisting with the annual society award. Facilitate and support student societies to operate effectively by following the School’s health and safety procedures and ensuring risk assessment is in place. Analysis & Reporting: Monitor and evaluate event performance according to key performance indicators by creating tracking mechanisms. Regularly produce detailed weekly, monthly, and annual reports for stakeholders. Leveraging attendee feedback to drive continuous improvement and highlight successes. Communication & Social Media: Collaboration with different stakeholders (Careers team, faculty, student ambassadors, marketing team, ExecEd team, programme content, etc) promoting their events & gathering user-generated content. Schedule and create social media content to showcase the student experience, contributing to London and cross-campus channels under the supervision and guidance of the Senior Digital Communications Manager and Federal Social Media Management team as well as the Senior CRCS Manager for communication-related to Careers Events. Develop and implement communication plans in liaison with key stakeholders and departmental colleagues to promote School and career events and societies. Monitoring and responding to student feedback, direct messaging, comments and social media posts in collaboration with the Senior Digital Communications Manager. Finance & Budgeting: Work with the Events and Student Experience Manager on the annual event budgets for the School. This includes budget allocation and reporting per event and an estimate of the number of events per year Liaise with Finance to manage event-related invoices and payments, ensuring effective cost management of events & purchase order processing, and accurate invoice tracking. Other Duties: Monitor new technology and trends in events and use insights to suggest new ways of working to support innovation Undertake regular competitor analysis and research industry trends to identify new opportunities. Person Specification Proven event management experience Flexibility to support events outside of 'office hours' Experience in events and social media-related roles Strong organisational and communication skills (written and verbal) High attention to detail and accuracy Ability to work both independently and collaboratively, managing multiple priorities under pressure Experience of budget management & cost control Effective at maintaining and growing networks with colleagues, stakeholders, and industry influencers Ability to work under pressure and prioritise workload to meet tight deadlines Excellent presentation skills with the ability to adapt to large and small scale Strong customer service approach & professionalism Experience with social media platforms & content creation Familiarity with SEO, analytics, web-traffic metrics and keyword search Experience using Adobe Creative software (Desirable) A Events-related qualication (Desirable) Benefits 30 days annual leave (pro rata) plus bank holidays Birthday leave Pension scheme with excellent employer contributions Réf: 24d26309-91f2-4269-9dca-e41d29b750fb Apply Events and Student Experience Executive (Maternity Cover) F/M ESCP Business School LONDON Temporary contract - 5 months Full time London 34083 GBP (£) - 35460 GBP (£) / year Title * Mrs. Mr. Mx Last name * First name * E-mail * Phone number * Availability * Select your availability immediate 2 weeks 1 month 2 months 3 months > 3 months Curriculum Vitae / Resume * Choose file Format: .PDF,  .DOCX, .DOC. Weight: max 2 MO. Do you currently have, or will you have, the right to work in the UK to undertake this role without requiring employer sponsorship? Please note that this role is not eligible for visa sponsorship. * Yes No Are you able to work on-site for the majority of the working week? Are you able to work flexibly to support events outside of standard 'office hours'? * Yes No How do you communicate effectively with various diverse stakeholders when managing an event? * Can you please describe an example of an event that you've managed  successfully and how you've owned the process from start to finish. * What is your current notice period? * As part of your application on the career site of ESCP Business School , the information you provide is processed for the review of your profile, on the basis of pre-contractual measures and the legitimate interest of the company in building a CV database. Some data may be automatically analysed (parsing and pre-screening) via an Artificial Intelligence system. No decision is made solely by AI, as every application is reviewed by a recruiter. Regarding the use of AI: - Your data is not retained by our AI solution. - It is not used to train an AI model. - Processing is carried out exclusively on servers located within the European Union. - No transfer outside the EU is carried out. Regarding your data: Unless otherwise requested, your data is retained for a maximum of 2 years. In accordance with our internal security policies (PSSI) and current best practices, robust technical and organisational measures are implemented to protect the access and integrity of your information: secure access, rights management, encryption, security protocols, access monitoring, employee awareness, etc. Regarding your rights: In accordance with the GDPR, you have the right to access, rectify, object to and delete your data. You may exercise these rights by contacting dpo@septeo.com. Apply Please answer to all required questions. Mandatory fields are followed by * * Required fields Share job Our last jobs Events and Student Experience Executive (Maternity Cover) F/M ESCP Business School London Campus Temporary contract\n- 5 months Full time London I apply Assistant / Associate Professor in Sustainability Management F/M ESCP Business School London Campus Permanent contract Full time London I apply Audiovisual Technician - Fixed-Term Contract F/H Temporary contract\n- 2 months Full time Paris I apply IT Development team manager F/H Permanent contract Full time Paris I apply See more jobs Follow us Jobs Spontaneous application Useful links Terms of Use Cookies Website map Recruiters access Consent choices Powered by Applicant Tracking System"
