    "https://careers.werecruit.io/en/escp-business-school/offers/assistant--associate-professor-in-sustainability-management-b29dce": {
      "title": "Assistant / Associate Professor in Sustainability Management F/M",
      "description": "Assistant / Associate Professor in Sustainability Management F/M - Permanent contract in London | Découvrez nos offres Menu Company page Espace Carrière & Mobilité des salariés ESCP Recrutement en Europe Site ESCP Plus See our jobs EN EN FR Company page Espace Carrière & Mobilité des salariés ESCP Recrutement en Europe Site ESCP EN EN FR See our jobs Assistant / Associate Professor in Sustainability Management F/M Apply to this job Assistant / Associate Professor in Sustainability Management F/M I apply Update on \n                14/10/2026 Subsidiary : ESCP Business School London Campus Contract type: Permanent contract Work time: Full time Location London Salary 59141 GBP (£) - 74240 GBP (£) / year About ESCP ESCP Business School is an international business school with campuses in 6 European metropolises. Founded in 1819, ESCP is the oldest business school in the world. To date, the business school is regularly awarded with top positions in the Financial Times rankings. Post description The Sustainability Department of ESCP Business School invites applications for one open-rank position at the Assistant or Associate Professor level (for entry-level positions, this role will follow the European Tenure Track process and expectations, noting local regulations). The position is based on our London campus and is to be filled by September 2027. Role Details Type of employment: Permanent Location: 527 Finchley Rd, London NW3 7BG Assistant Professor Salary range: £59,141 - £64,426 Associate Professor Salary Range: £65,432 - £74,240 The Sustainability Department is composed of a multi-disciplinary team of 19 full-time faculty and 7 affiliate professors that have developed a strong expertise in sustainability integrating various fields of origin: organization theory, supply chain management, business model design, governance, responsible and sustainable consumption, among others. We have varied research interests, backgrounds and methodological approaches but we are all striving for an uncompromising ambition to change business research, curricula and practice. We protect principles of diversity, inclusion, and academic freedom. Our faculty are publishing in leading academic journals such as the Academy of Management Annals, Journal of Management Studies, Organization Studies, Journal of Business Ethics, Business Strategy and the Environment, Journal of World Business, Ecological Economics, Journal of Consumer Research, PNAS, among others. Applications should include: A cover letter. Your curriculum vitae with a list of publications. Your “sustainability statement as a scholar” sharing your vision and your personal way of embodying the role of academic in sustainability management Teaching evaluations from the past two years (if applicable). Two references (providing contact details will be enough at the initial application stage). The closing date for applications is 15th November 2026 . For further information, please contact Professor Joe Miemczyk, jmiemczyk@escp.eu Profile required We are looking for candidates with a PhD and a track record of publications and/or promising academic submissions in top-quality international journals in the Sustainability Management field, who will actively contribute to research, teaching, and program coordination in this area. Ideally, candidates would also be able to teach operations and supply chain fundamental courses. Candidates should demonstrate excellent teaching capabilities, a strong collaborative mindset. Candidates must have a sound foundation in sustainability and should be able to teach courses covering both, major sustainability challenges (e.g. climate change and social impacts etc.), and sustainability management in organizations (e.g. governance, sustainable business models, etc.). For operations classes the candidate should be comfortable with teaching operations and supply chain models and frameworks. Teaching should address various audiences, from undergraduates to executives. Benefits 30 days annual leave, plus bank holidays Birthday Leave Company pension scheme with excellent employer contributions Optional private Dental and Medical cover (after completion of 6 months service) Hybrid working available Réf: b29dcef2-9d1b-4c06-8bf1-d84e09923023 Apply Assistant / Associate Professor in Sustainability Management F/M ESCP Business School LONDON Permanent contract Full time London 59141 GBP (£) - 74240 GBP (£) / year Title * Mrs. Mr. Mx Last name * First name * E-mail * Phone number * Availability * Select your availability immediate 2 weeks 1 month 2 months 3 months > 3 months Teaching evaluations from the past two years (if applicable) Choose file Format: .PDF,  .DOCX, .DOC. Weight: max 2 MO. Curriculum vitae * Choose file Format: .PDF,  .DOCX, .DOC. Weight: max 2 MO. Statement - Your “sustainability statement as a scholar” sharing your vision and your personal way of embodying the role of academic in sustainability management * Choose file Format: .PDF,  .DOCX, .DOC. Weight: max 2 MO. Two references - Contact details * Choose file Format: .PDF,  .DOCX, .DOC. Weight: max 2 MO. List of publications * Choose file Format: .PDF,  .DOCX, .DOC. Weight: max 2 MO. Cover Letter * Choose file Format: .PDF,  .DOCX, .DOC. Weight: max 2 MO. Do you have the right to work in the UK? * Yes No For candidates without current UK right to work status, please outline the route  you will be seeking to gain the right to work and whether any employer support would be needed. This role is within scope for sponsorship, if required. Are you PHD qualified? * Yes No Have you submitted all the required documents outlined in the job advert? (If your documents exceed the available file size limit, please email any additional supporting documents to ukrecruitment@escp.eu) * Yes No As part of your application on the career site of ESCP Business School , the information you provide is processed for the review of your profile, on the basis of pre-contractual measures and the legitimate interest of the company in building a CV database. Some data may be automatically analysed (parsing and pre-screening) via an Artificial Intelligence system. No decision is made solely by AI, as every application is reviewed by a recruiter. Regarding the use of AI: - Your data is not retained by our AI solution. - It is not used to train an AI model. - Processing is carried out exclusively on servers located within the European Union. - No transfer outside the EU is carried out. Regarding your data: Unless otherwise requested, your data is retained for a maximum of 2 years. In accordance with our internal security policies (PSSI) and current best practices, robust technical and organisational measures are implemented to protect the access and integrity of your information: secure access, rights management, encryption, security protocols, access monitoring, employee awareness, etc. Regarding your rights: In accordance with the GDPR, you have the right to access, rectify, object to and delete your data. You may exercise these rights by contacting dpo@septeo.com. Apply Please answer to all required questions. Mandatory fields are followed by * * Required fields Share job Our last jobs Events and Student Experience Executive (Maternity Cover) F/M ESCP Business School London Campus Temporary contract\n- 5 months Full time London I apply Assistant / Associate Professor in Sustainability Management F/M ESCP Business School London Campus Permanent contract Full time London I apply Audiovisual Technician - Fixed-Term Contract F/H Temporary contract\n- 2 months Full time Paris I apply IT Development team manager F/H Permanent contract Full time Paris I apply See more jobs Follow us Jobs Spontaneous application Useful links Terms of Use Cookies Website map Recruiters access Consent choices Powered by Applicant Tracking System"
