    "https://careers.werecruit.io/en/escp-business-school/offers/it-development-team-manager-de9e21": {
      "title": "IT Development team manager F/H",
      "description": "IT Development team manager F/H - Permanent contract in Paris | Découvrez nos offres With your agreement, We Recruit and our partners use cookies or similar technologies to store, access, and process personal data like your visit on this website, IP addresses and cookie identifiers. Some partners do not ask for your consent to process your data and rely on their legitimate business interest. You can withdraw your consent or object to data processing based on legitimate interest at any time by clicking on “Learn More” or in our Privacy Policy on this website. View our 8 partners Learn More → Disagree and close Agree and close Menu Company page Espace Carrière & Mobilité des salariés ESCP Plus Recrutement en Europe Site ESCP See our jobs EN EN FR Company page Espace Carrière & Mobilité des salariés ESCP Recrutement en Europe Site ESCP EN Retour EN EN FR See our jobs IT Development team manager F/H Apply to this job IT Development team manager F/H I apply Update on \n                15/10/2026 Contract type: Permanent contract Work time: Full time Location Paris The company ESCP Business School is the world-renowned business school, founded in 1819, that trains the responsible leaders of tomorrow. Located in the heart of Paris, it offers innovative and multicultural teaching, supported by a network of six European campuses. Recognized for the excellence of its management programs, it fosters engagement, international awareness, and personalized support for talent throughout their studies. Post description Team management and development Lead and coordinate the team, set individual and collective objectives, and support their achievement using the SMART framework. Assess and develop technical and interpersonal skills (hard and soft skills), identify training needs, and support the development of technical and methodological expertise. Contribute to recruitment and onboarding by defining candidate profiles, participating in interviews, and facilitating the integration of new team members. Foster team cohesion by creating a motivating and collaborative working environment that encourages knowledge sharing and technical discussions among peers. Provide ongoing support to team members, helping resolve challenges and encouraging collective progress. Facilitate Agile ceremonies, including daily stand-ups, sprints, and team meetings. Activity and delivery management Maintain an Agile working environment that enables the regular delivery of new operational services to the School's user communities. Plan and coordinate development cycles, priorities, and maintenance activities in alignment with management objectives and ESCP Business School's strategy. Manage capacity planning by assessing available resources, anticipating needs, distributing workloads, and ensuring delivery commitments are met. Ensure an appropriate balance between third-level support activities and new development initiatives. Prepare or validate estimates of workloads, timelines, resources, costs, and risks. Ensure deliverable quality through compliance with coding standards, security best practices, and testing procedures. Define and monitor key performance indicators to track project progress and achievement of objectives. Produce regular progress reports for management and relevant stakeholders. Technical management and architecture Facilitate collaborative technical decision-making and contribute to validating technology choices, frameworks, and development tools in alignment with the Information Systems strategy. Oversee technical design, development, integration, testing, and production deployment in coordination with the team. Contribute to reducing technical debt by planning refactoring initiatives, corrective maintenance, and continuous code improvement. Ensure the quality of technical documentation, version management, application performance, and reliability. Monitor technological developments, anticipate emerging trends, and recommend improvements that address business and user needs. Communication and cross-functional collaboration Act as the main point of contact for business teams regarding the service's functional scope, working closely with other department managers. Collaborate with other teams within the Business Solutions Department and the DSIN. Actively contribute to implementing the service's communication plan. Participate in Business Solutions Department management meetings. Prepare and deliver presentations on achievements, operational activities, and project progress for relevant governance committees. Required Skills and Technical Environment Development primarily using Symfony (PHP). Familiarity with Django (Python). Talend. PostgreSQL and Oracle databases. Linux and Windows environments. Use of AI tools, including OpenAI Codex and Claude. Use of Monday.com for activity tracking and coordination. Knowledge of agile methodologies. Profile required Technical expertise Strong knowledge of the development environments and technology stacks used at ESCP Business School, ideally complemented by significant experience in Full Stack development. At least 10 years of experience in software testing, version control, and supporting production deployments. Proven ability to produce clear and comprehensive technical documentation. Team management and coordination At least 4 years of direct line management experience, supervising a team of at least four people, ideally within a software development environment using Agile methodologies. Ability to organize and coordinate multiple activities, plan actions, and allocate the resources required for successful delivery. Ability to establish priorities, support team members, and facilitate collaboration across stakeholders. Interpersonal and organizational skills Availability, active listening skills, and ability to provide ongoing support to teams. A structured and methodical approach to work organization, activity monitoring, and meeting commitments. Strong service orientation and commitment to meeting user needs. Ability to prioritize effectively and communicate clearly with a wide range of stakeholders. Languages and mobility French: Professional proficiency is essential, as French is the primary working language. English: Good professional proficiency is required to work effectively in a European environment and collaborate with teams across campuses. Occasional travel may be required to other ESCP Business School European campuses: Turin, Madrid, London, and Berlin. Required languages English - Level advanced Réf: de9e2150-fb42-477d-b68a-863d6ec1dcc7 Apply IT Development team manager F/H Permanent contract Full time Paris Title * Mrs. Mr. Mx Last name * First name * E-mail * Phone number * Availability * Select your availability immediate 2 weeks 1 month 2 months 3 months > 3 months Salary expectations (Gross/year) * Select a salary expectation Inferior than 15 000€ 15 000€ - 20 000€ 20 000€ - 25 000€ 25 000€ - 30 000€ 30 000€ - 35 000€ 35 000€ - 40 000€ 40 000€ - 45 000€ 45 000€ - 50 000€ 50 000€ - 55 000€ 55 000€ - 60 000€ 60 000€ - 65 000€ 65 000€ - 70 000€ 70 000€ - 75 000€ 75 000€ - 80 000€ 80 000€ - 85 000€ Superior than 85 000€ Photo Choose file Format: JPG \nWeight: max 2 MO. Resume * Choose file Format: .PDF,  .DOCX, .DOC. Weight: max 2 MO. Quel est votre niveau d'anglais ? * Select an answer Beginner Intermediary Advanced Bilingual Pourquoi souhaitez vous rejoindre ESCP Business School ? As part of your application on the career site of ESCP Business School , the information you provide is processed for the review of your profile, on the basis of pre-contractual measures and the legitimate interest of the company in building a CV database. Some data may be automatically analysed (parsing and pre-screening) via an Artificial Intelligence system. No decision is made solely by AI, as every application is reviewed by a recruiter. Regarding the use of AI: - Your data is not retained by our AI solution. - It is not used to train an AI model. - Processing is carried out exclusively on servers located within the European Union. - No transfer outside the EU is carried out. Regarding your data: Unless otherwise requested, your data is retained for a maximum of 2 years. In accordance with our internal security policies (PSSI) and current best practices, robust technical and organisational measures are implemented to protect the access and integrity of your information: secure access, rights management, encryption, security protocols, access monitoring, employee awareness, etc. Regarding your rights: In accordance with the GDPR, you have the right to access, rectify, object to and delete your data. You may exercise these rights by contacting dpo@septeo.com. Apply Please answer to all required questions. Mandatory fields are followed by * * Required fields Share job Our last jobs Events and Student Experience Executive (Maternity Cover) F/M ESCP Business School London Campus Temporary contract\n- 5 months Full time London I apply Assistant / Associate Professor in Sustainability Management F/M ESCP Business School London Campus Permanent contract Full time London I apply Audiovisual Technician - Fixed-Term Contract F/H Temporary contract\n- 2 months Full time Paris I apply IT Development team manager F/H Permanent contract Full time Paris I apply See more jobs Follow us Jobs Spontaneous application Useful links Terms of Use Cookies Website map Recruiters access Consent choices Powered by Applicant Tracking System"
