      "description": "European Financial Controller – Infrastructure and Campus Life F/H - Permanent contract in Paris | Découvrez nos offres With your agreement, We Recruit and our partners use cookies or similar technologies to store, access, and process personal data like your visit on this website, IP addresses and cookie identifiers. Some partners do not ask for your consent to process your data and rely on their legitimate business interest. You can withdraw your consent or object to data processing based on legitimate interest at any time by clicking on “Learn More” or in our Privacy Policy on this website. View our 8 partners Learn More → Disagree and close Agree and close Menu Company page Espace Carrière & Mobilité des salariés ESCP Plus Recrutement en Europe Site ESCP See our jobs EN EN FR Company page Espace Carrière & Mobilité des salariés ESCP Recrutement en Europe Site ESCP EN Retour EN EN FR See our jobs European Financial Controller – Infrastructure and Campus Life F/H Apply to this job European Financial Controller – Infrastructure and Campus Life F/H I apply Published on               \n                09/10/2026 Contract type: Permanent contract Work time: Full time Location Paris The company ESCP Business School is the world-renowned business school, founded in 1819, that trains the responsible leaders of tomorrow. Located in the heart of Paris, it offers innovative and multicultural teaching, supported by a network of six European campuses. Recognized for the excellence of its management programs, it fosters engagement, international awareness, and personalized support for talent throughout their studies. Post description ESCP is seeking a professional to lead European financial control and support, as a Business Partner, the Infrastructure, Real Estate, IT and Campus Life departments. In a context of transformation and major investments—nearly €300 million over five years—the role contributes to monitoring the financial performance of operations and investments, linking financial considerations with service quality and the student experience. Responsibilities Support the Real Estate, IT and Campus Life departments in their budgeting, forecasting and investment decisions. Build business cases and financial models for real estate and technology projects, and monitor their ROI. Monitor budget execution, commitments, cash outflows and project costs across multiple campuses. Develop indicators combining financial data, service usage and student satisfaction. Produce analyses for Senior Management and contribute to decision-making and resource allocation. Harmonise practices and improve reporting, business intelligence and data analytics tools. Profile required Required Skills and Experience Degree in finance from a leading business or engineering school or university. 5 to 10 years’ experience in management control within a demanding environment, a Big Four audit firm or transaction services. Excellent skills in management control, financial analysis and financial modelling. Proven experience in business partnering is essential; international and matrix-environment experience is desirable. Ability to communicate complex information, formulate recommendations and support decision-making. Ability to organise one’s workload and priorities, demonstrate initiative and work rigorously. Fluent professional English and excellent understanding of financial issues. Interest in investments, real estate and transformation projects within an international environment. Required languages English - Level Bilingual Réf: 98f9405b-b33d-493d-8c6c-453fb2486569 Apply European Financial Controller – Infrastructure and Campus Life F/H Permanent contract Full time Paris Title * Mrs. Mr. Mx Last name * First name * E-mail * Phone number * Availability * Select your availability immediate 2 weeks 1 month 2 months 3 months > 3 months Salary expectations (Gross/year) * Select a salary expectation Inferior than 15 000€ 15 000€ - 20 000€ 