      "title": "European Financial Controller",
      "description": "European Financial Controller – Initial Education BU F/H - Permanent contract in Paris | Découvrez nos offres With your agreement, We Recruit and our partners use cookies or similar technologies to store, access, and process personal data like your visit on this website, IP addresses and cookie identifiers. Some partners do not ask for your consent to process your data and rely on their legitimate business interest. You can withdraw your consent or object to data processing based on legitimate interest at any time by clicking on “Learn More” or in our Privacy Policy on this website. View our 8 partners Learn More → Disagree and close Agree and close Menu Company page Espace Carrière & Mobilité des salariés ESCP Plus Recrutement en Europe Site ESCP See our jobs EN EN FR Company page Espace Carrière & Mobilité des salariés ESCP Recrutement en Europe Site ESCP EN Retour EN EN FR See our jobs European Financial Controller – Initial Education BU F/H Apply to this job European Financial Controller – Initial Education BU F/H I apply Update on \n                12/10/2026 Contract type: Permanent contract Work time: Full time Location Paris The company ESCP Business School is the world-renowned business school, founded in 1819, that trains the responsible leaders of tomorrow. Located in the heart of Paris, it offers innovative and multicultural teaching, supported by a network of six European campuses. Recognized for the excellence of its management programs, it fosters engagement, international awareness, and personalized support for talent throughout their studies. Post description Within the Group Finance Department, the Financial Controller serves as the financial reference for the Initial Education Business Unit (Bachelor, Master in Management, MSc and MBA). In a multi-campus and international environment, the position supports Academic Management as a finance business partner. The role contributes to the financial performance monitoring of the programmes and provides the analyses required to support strategic decisions, with the aim of optimising resources and ensuring the sustainability of the academic model. Responsibilities Prepare, consolidate and monitor the budgets and forecasts of the Initial Education BU across all campuses. Produce monthly reports, analyse variances and provide operational recommendations. Define and monitor key financial indicators, including cost per student, programme profitability and campus contribution. Support Programme Management and Academic Management in their financial forecasts and decision-making, including the analysis of options relating to the development of specialisations and programmes, locations, etc. Build financial models and business plans for new programmes and academic projects. Coordinate financial processes across campuses and ensure the reliability of data and reporting. Develop financial monitoring tools and contribute to cross-functional projects related to ERP systems, business intelligence, planning and data. Profile required Required Skills and Experience Degree in finance from a leading business or engineering school or university. 5 to 8 years’ experience in management control within a demanding environment, transaction services or a Big Four audit firm. Proven experience in business partnering is essential; international and matrix-environment experience is desirable. Excellent knowledge of management control, financial modelling, Excel and BI tools; knowledge of an ERP system is a plus. Excellent command of professional English and of financial and accounting terminology, particularly IFRS standards. Ability to produce structured financial analyses and implement the necessary actions to achieve objectives. Ability to engage with non-financial stakeholders, present complex information and formulate recommendations. Ability to organise one’s workload, set priorities and manage responsibilities independently in a multi-campus environment. Ability to demonstrate initiative and propose solutions tailored to the challenges encountered. Required languages English - Level Bilingual Réf: aed00a7a-07e2-4f2d-b468-979690dead08 Apply European Financial Controller – Initial Education BU F/H Permanent contract Full time Paris Title * Mrs. Mr. Mx Last name * First name * E-mail * Phone number * Availability * Select your availability immediate 2 weeks 1 month 2 months 3 months > 3 months Salary expectations (Gross/year) * Select a salary expectation Inferior than 15 000€ 15 000€ - 20 000€ 20 000€ - 25 000€ 25 000€ - 30 000€ 30 000€ - 35 000€ 35 000€ - 40 000€ 40 000€ - 45 000€ 45 000€ - 50 000€ 50 000€ - 55 000€ 55 000€ - 60 000€ 60 000€ - 65 000€ 65 000€ - 70 000€ 70 000€ - 75 000€ 75 000€ - 80 000€ 80 000€ - 85 000€ Superior than 85 000€ Photo Choose file Format: JPG \nWeight: max 2 MO. Resume * Choose file Format: .PDF,  .DOCX, .DOC. Weight: max 2 MO. Quel est votre niveau d'anglais ? * Select an answer Beginner Intermediary Advanced Bilingual Quelles sont vos motivations pour rejoindre ESCP Business school Quelle est votre compréhension du poste que nous proposons ? * As part of your application on the career site of ESCP Business School , the information you provide is processed for the review of your profile, on the basis of pre-contractual measures and the legitimate interest of the company in building a CV database. Some data may be automatically analysed (parsing and pre-screening) via an Artificial Intelligence system. No decision is made solely by AI, as every application is reviewed by a recruiter. Regarding the use of AI: - Your data is not retained by our AI solution. - It is not used to train an AI model. - Processing is carried out exclusively on servers located within the European Union. - No transfer outside the EU is carried out. Regarding your data: Unless otherwise requested, your data is retained for a maximum of 2 years. In accordance with our internal security policies (PSSI) and current best pract